Keep the groove border of the scroll bar under the thin key

The writer dropped the border of the scroll bar groove whenever
the borderSbarGroove key was false. The style suppresses that
border inside Style::drawLightBevelReal() for WIDGET_TROUGH
alone. The groove call of Style::drawComplexControl() passes
WIDGET_TROUGH only when thinSbarGroove is false, and the page
paths never reach the suppression. Under the thin groove the
style therefore keeps the border that the sheet dropped.

Writer::scrollBar() now drops the border only when neither
groove key holds, which mirrors the one reachable gate.

assert-scrollbar.sh moves the noborder arm into the border arms
and adds the bare arm, which holds the two keys at false and
expects no border. The two arms carry one control each.

The change sits on the branch work/gtk4-theme of the local tree, as the
fifteenth commit. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !15
on system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/gtk4/check/assert-scrollbar.sh b/gtk4/check/assert-scrollbar.sh
index 7448af82..e1ee7c01 100644
--- a/gtk4/check/assert-scrollbar.sh
+++ b/gtk4/check/assert-scrollbar.sh
@@ -47,16 +47,16 @@ edge="1px solid shade($base, 0.750)"
 custom='#ff8800'
 
 # Every arm of the light scheme, in the order that the run writes them. The
-# last two arms take no colour name. The noborder arm drops the border of the
+# last three arms take no colour name. The noborder arm keeps the border of the
 # trough, and the hsv arm writes a literal for every shaded tone.
 arms='none darken selected blend custom mo slapp app thin wide page corner
-      square noborder hsv'
+      square noborder bare hsv'
 # The arms that hold a colour name in the trough rule.
 namearms='none darken selected blend custom mo slapp app thin wide page corner
-          square noborder'
+          square noborder bare'
 # The arms that hold the border of the trough on a colour name.
 edgearms='none darken selected blend custom mo slapp app thin wide page corner
-          square'
+          square noborder'
 # The arms of the distinct scheme, where no two roles share a value.
 darms='none blend hsv'
 
@@ -101,8 +101,10 @@ settings page 'flatSbarButtons=false\nthinSbarGroove=true\n'
 settings corner 'flatSbarButtons=false\nthinSbarGroove=true\nscrollbarType=none\n'
 settings square \
     'flatSbarButtons=false\nthinSbarGroove=true\nscrollbarType=none\nround=none\n'
-# The border key of the groove, which drops the border of the trough.
+# The border key of the groove alone, which keeps the border of the trough.
 settings noborder 'borderSbarGroove=false\n'
+# The two groove keys at false, which drop the border of the trough.
+settings bare 'borderSbarGroove=false\nthinSbarGroove=false\n'
 # The shading model of the sheet. The GTK function shade() computes the HSL
 # model alone, so another model gives a literal for every shaded tone. Each
 # seed then stands as a byte that a reader can measure.
@@ -268,7 +270,7 @@ check() {
     fi
 
     # 7. The border of the trough takes the border step of the base ladder,
-    # and the border key of the groove drops it.
+    # and the two groove keys drop it only together.
     for c_arm in $edgearms; do
         if [ "$(row "$d" "$c_arm" "$trough" border)" != "$edge" ]; then
             echo "assert-scrollbar: the trough of $c_arm borders on" \
@@ -276,8 +278,8 @@ check() {
             return 1
         fi
     done
-    if [ "$(row "$d" noborder "$trough" border)" != none ]; then
-        echo "assert-scrollbar: the noborder arm keeps the border of the" \
+    if [ "$(row "$d" bare "$trough" border)" != none ]; then
+        echo "assert-scrollbar: the bare arm keeps the border of the" \
              "trough" >&2
         return 1
     fi
@@ -325,7 +327,7 @@ check() {
     # 10. The block of the browser reads the same helper. Its ground must hold
     # the trough of the widget, and its rest row must hold the thumb of the
     # widget. The clause holds only where the sheet carries that block, which
-    # assert-browser.sh reads. The rest clause reads the arms 1 to 14. Under
+    # assert-browser.sh reads. The rest clause reads the arms 1 to 15. Under
     # the hsv arm the widget rest row writes the literal of its cover branch
     # and the block writes the colour name. The two spellings give one colour.
     if [ -n "$(row "$d" none "$moz" background-color)" ]; then
@@ -427,10 +429,16 @@ paste hsv "$trough" background-color \
     "$(row "$work/arm" hsv "$anchor" background-color)"
 control 'the seed of the trough'
 
-# The border of the noborder arm at a line, which the border key drops.
-paste noborder "$trough" border "$edge"
+# The border of the noborder arm at none, which is the sheet of the writer
+# that reads the border key alone.
+paste noborder "$trough" border none
 control 'the border key of the groove'
 
+# The border of the bare arm at a line, which is the sheet of a writer that
+# never drops the border.
+paste bare "$trough" border "$edge"
+control 'the two keys of the groove'
+
 # The border of the thumb of the selected arm on the button ladder, which is
 # the border of another fill.
 paste selected "$thumb" border "1px solid shade($button, 0.750)"
diff --git a/gtk4/writer/widgets.cpp b/gtk4/writer/widgets.cpp
index 14b5d7f1..f3613a94 100644
--- a/gtk4/writer/widgets.cpp
+++ b/gtk4/writer/widgets.cpp
@@ -1644,7 +1644,9 @@ Writer::scrollBar()
     trough.image = tgrad(QStringLiteral("sbar-trough-img"),
                          m_opts.grooveAppearance, scrollTone(spec.track));
     trough.bg = tv(QStringLiteral("sbar-trough-bg"), scrollTone(spec.track));
-    trough.border = m_opts.borderSbarGroove ?
+    // The style drops this border for the wide groove alone, so the border
+    // falls only when neither groove key holds.
+    trough.border = (m_opts.borderSbarGroove || m_opts.thinSbarGroove) ?
         tline(QStringLiteral("sbar-trough-border"),
               lad(Role::Base, QTC_STD_BORDER)) :
         v(QStringLiteral("sbar-trough-noborder"), QStringLiteral("none"));
